      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T18:17:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this check doesn\u0027t match, doesn\u0027t that mean there\u0027s a bug? Should we be panicking rather than just putting this inside a conditional?\n\nIf not, is it only an option of having 0 modules sometimes?\n\nMostly, this code looks like it will silently do something unusual if we manage to have len(sharedLibrariesModules) \u003d\u003d 2 and len(sharedLibararies) \u003d\u003d 3 or something like that.\n\nNormally, wanting to do this kind of indexing would instead make me think that `sharedLibraries` should instead be a tuple of a path and a module.\n\nIf there\u0027s an intentionally supported case where the module is not available, then it can be a module pointer instead with nil used to encode a missing module.",
      "revId": "deca46257e5bb1f501fee8ec7572eac761d99eeb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
